  {
   "id": "princess-farmer-134882@major-2021-06-12",
   "gameId": "princess-farmer-134882",
   "displayName": "First Big Demo Update!",
   "kind": "major",
   "kindBasis": "studio",
   "announcedAt": "2021-06-12T17:00:16.000Z",
   "notes": [
    {
     "title": "First big update since the demo launched!",
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "A big warning: your saved progress, including hare dye purchases and heart coins, is going to get wiped. There were just too many updates to fundamental things to be able to keep old saves working. It's still in very active development, after all!",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "Major Updates",
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "New level balancing! We noticed there are generally 2 types of players: people who like to go fast and just zone out, and people who ponder each move and take their time with it. And so Soft Bunny/Tough Bunny/Diamond Bunny are now Action Bunny/Puzzle Bunny/Balanced Bunny! And all three are unlocked right from the start! Pick Action Bunny if you want breezy levels and not have to plan too much, pick Puzzle Bunny if you prefer to spend time to plan your moves to maximize whatever the level's goal is, and pick Balanced Bunny if you want a mix of both.",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "new"
      },
      {
       "text": "Goal Deets! (That's what my wife called them so I just stuck with it) Since we've added more complex goals and things to avoid, we also added this UI element to give you a visual reminder of what you should be focusing on. You'll find two boxes right under your Stack UI at the (usually) right side of the board. The green box means you should aim for that to maximize your reward, and the red box means that's what you want to avoid (unless it's time. You can't avoid time. Sadly.)",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      },
      {
       "text": "Return to Cottage! Once you've bought some cool new hare dyes from Ro's Shoppe, you can now access Return to Cottage from the pause menu (Esc on keyboard and Start on controller) so you can change into them right away! Don't worry though; once you leave the cottage you can get back to where you left off when you open up your map.",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": true,
       "category": "other",
       "platforms": [
        "pc"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "Minor Updates/Fixes",
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "Lots! But let us know if you come across any bugs at contact@samobee.com or on the Whitethorn Discord.",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "fixed"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
